<p>Neutral&#8230; for now.</p>
<p>I'm not sure what to think of this one. I like it. But I'm not sure what to think yet. Maybe that's part of it&#8230; weird for weird's sake? That'd be okay. But I feel like there is a deeper meaning here, and I want to figure it out before I vote, so I will be reading this again soon.</p>
<p>EDIT: So I reread this, and I'm afraid I have to remain neutral. I don't understand what's happening here&#8230; and when I know I don't understand an article, I vote neutral. There's a hook, what with them being siblings, with the deaths, with what you said about them thinking their plants, but either I'm too dense to understand it, or it's not clear enough. I would suggest you add a tiny little bit more of a nudge into what's happening here in the skip itself, because as it stands, I'm not sure anyone here gets it. If not, that's fine, I still think its cool and creepy and mysterious. Just one thing I've been dying to ask though,</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Site-49 has been constructed around SCP-2157 for the purposes of containing and studying it under the public pretense of an agriculture research outpost. Guards armed with light weapons are to patrol the exterior of the site and deter civilian approach.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>What kind of &quot;agriculture research outpost&quot; has armed guards patrolling the exterior of the building? It sounds like these things cause no compulsion to get people to join them, so I doubt that's really necessary. The guards probably cause more questions than they deter.</p>

